From cff98be4310dad70567ca383721df5ee62bf11b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Cache with proof: ctypes.util.find_library's `ldconfig
 -p` reads the linker cache (not a subprocess); walk: --det-urandom, units
 that cannot be collected left out and listed, output tails kept; pylint
 without pytest-benchmark, home-assistant with --continue-on-collection-errors

* ifaddr (Home Assistant) calls find_library at import time: every test was "subprocess"; now
  /etc/ld.so.cache is a data input (test fails before, passes after)
* r3: every Home Assistant shard ended with exit 2 (one test module or conftest that cannot be imported
  because the installer dropped its requirement aborts the session)
* pytest-benchmark runs git in pytest_addoption: a startup spawn makes every test uncacheable (pylint smoke:
  2,494 of 2,495), reported; the pylint walk disables the plugin (its tests are ignored anyway)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAF6Dgp7MTxUYBRZseFL3V
